{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-commutative-formal-group","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:commutative-formal-group","kind":"definition","title":"Commutative formal group","cites":["references/hazewinkel1978"],"tags":["formal-group","commutative","characteristic-p"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup","text":"commutative-formal-group.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/commutative-formal-group.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:commutative-formal-group\"></a><p>A <strong>commutative formal group</strong> over a field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> of characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>\nis a formal group law <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F \\colon \\mathcal{O}(H) \\times \\mathcal{O}(H) \\to \\mathcal{O}(H)</code>\nsatisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F(X, Y) = F(Y, X)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F(X, 0) = X</code>.</p>\n<p>This is the base object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H / \\mathbb{F}_p</code> in the dissertation's\nintegration theorem.  It carries a coordinate ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}(H)</code>\nand a commutative formal group law.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"hazewinkel1978\">[hazewinkel1978]</span>, Chapter I.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/commutative-formal-group.md","heading":"Definition","number":"1.1.1"}
